  "description": "Register, sign in and sign out for a Rask app, on by default. Accounts are the app's own User aggregate (PBKDF2 or bcrypt password hashing, one revocable session row per signed-in device, sign-in throttling) and are exposed through Rask's own host-neutral surface — the same IUserProvider, Authorize component and [Authorize] routes work unchanged on the Server, WebAssembly, island, SPA and meta-framework hosts. rask new writes the /login, /register, /logout and /devices pages into the app, and the matching /api/auth endpoints give a TypeScript front end the same flows. Email confirmation and password reset go out through the app's own mail queue, with /confirm-email, /forgot-password and /reset-password pages scaffolded to match. The first account to register becomes the admin.",
